# Everything here is sent to the Docker daemon before the first layer is
# built, whether or not a COPY names it. On a working tree that has run the
# AI provisioning that came to about 4.5GB -- model weights, a virtualenv
# and the git history -- for an image that copies a few megabytes.
#
# Excludes only. No `!` re-includes: the build must stay readable, and the
# test that checks no COPY source is excluded relies on it.

.git
.venv
.AImodels
vendor
tests
docs
benchmarks
probes
assets
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
*.log
*.bak

# experiments/ is deliberately kept: `make build_exp` copies its
# smartgallery.py and templates/ instead of the ones at the root.
